WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.980
JENNY BROWN: And we're back.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.470
Today we're talking about
the new Cloud Operations

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.250
Sandbox, data security
strategies, and a new AppSheet

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.360
tutorial.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.420
I'm Jenny Brown, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.050
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.930
Cloud Operations Sandbox
is an open source tool

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.900
that helps you learn SRE
practices from Google,

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.900
and then apply them on Cloud
Services using Google Cloud's

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.400
operations suite.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.240
It's got everything you need to
get started in just one click.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.740
So be sure to check out the
blog post for more information.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.000
Our new whitepaper
explores the questions

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.540
of building a data security
program in a Cloud-native way,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.390
and of adapting an
existing program to utilize

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.220
Cloud computing services.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.190
Read the blog post for more
best practices and background

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.150
information, or download the
paper to learn for yourself.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.180
AppSheet is Google Cloud's
no-code app development

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:54.990
platform.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.060
And this tutorial
walks you through it

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.310
by building a
usable fitness app.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.530
And more importantly,
it provides you

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.210
the skills to
build any app you'd

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.519
like without needing to code.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:08.830
A new year is a great chance
to learn something new.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.620
And I recently had
the opportunity

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.920
to learn directly from Cassie
Kozyrkov, our head of Decision

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.210
Intelligence.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.860
Check out the
podcast to hear more

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.600
about the role of
decision-makers,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.427
your intuition, and
data in decision-making.

00:01:22.427 --> 00:01:24.510
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.370
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:30.700
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.930
We'll see you in the Cloud.

